From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:06:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: achievement diary journals for all areas; Lumbridge &
 Draynor and Varrock task progress (11 tasks)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Only two diaries had a journal, and no diary task progress was tracked.

Change.
- Journals for the other 10 areas (Ardougne, Desert, Falador, Fremennik, Kandarin, Karamja,
  Morytania, Western Provinces, Wilderness, Kourend & Kebos), worded and laid out as the game
  sends them, including each diary's own spacer lines (Karamja and Kourend use "" spacers,
  Ardougne a double " ", Kourend ends open tasks with "</col>") and the red "(Requires ...)" /
  "(Does not require task)" notes.
- Task progress for 11 Lumbridge & Draynor / Varrock tasks, through hooks in Hans (Age),
  the sawmill, cooking (bread on the Lumbridge range), firemaking (oak), spell teleports,
  runecrafting (water/earth from essence) and the essence mine teleports (Sedridor, Aubury).
- As captured, completing a task sends on the same tick the chat message "<col=dc143c>Well
  done! You have completed an easy task in the <area> area. Your Achievement Diary has been
  updated.</col>" ("a medium", "a hard", "an elite"), the tier's <area>_<tier>_count varbit and,
  on the diary's first task, started_<area>_diary; the journal strikes the task.
- 3 ticks after a tier's last task its <area>_diary_<tier>_complete varbit is set and a message
  box says "Congratulations! You have completed all of the <tier> tasks in the <area> area.
  Speak to <NPC> to claim your reward." (Hatius Cosaintus east of Lumbridge Castle; Toby behind
  the general store in Varrock). The box waits until the player is free. The journal's tier
  heading turns green with that varbit.
- On login the count, started and complete varbits are re-sent from the server bits.

Tests. DiaryTasksTest (integration): every captured journal (all 12) rebuilt line for line from
the progress it shows; opening a journal sets pagepos and busy and closing clears busy; a task
counts once and sets the client varbits; the captured chat message; the tier-complete varbit 3
ticks after the last task, with the box; oak logs cut and burned in Lumbridge; done tasks struck.

Data sources.
- Task lists and order: OSRS Wiki, the 12 diary pages (task tables and Changes).
- Task wording, journal layout, the task-complete message, the tier-complete delay and box,
  the login varbits: rsprox captures (opening every diary, completing Ardougne easy tasks) as
  recorded by TSPS (https://github.com/RSPSApp/tsps, a TypeScript OSRS server whose content is
  reconstructed from rsprox captures): docs/achievement-diaries.md,
  server/plugins/achievements/diaries/data/achievement-diaries.json and
  server/tests/fixtures/achievement-diary-journals.json (the test's fixture, diary-journals.txt,
  is that capture).
- Varbits (started, count, complete): cache gamevals.

Caveats.
- Per-task bits are in server varps 63787-63794 (63795: the oak-cut step); the real
  *_achievement_diary bit layout is not mapped (no cache script reads it).
- The message's and box's area names for Lumbridge & Draynor and Varrock follow the captured
  Ardougne ones by analogy; the reward NPC wording in the box is captured for Ardougne only, the
  two used here follow the Wiki's description of where the NPC stands.
- No rewards (claiming, reward varbits, the journal's "If I ever lose my ..." reminders).
- Area boxes (Lumbridge, the Al Kharid mine) are approximate.
- In CookingEvents.kt the hook is added after main's own "You successfully cook" message.

